A||||31||TRiAD||OK, how's about some hard-core 3800SC info?||||5||
Z||000000||TRiAD||06-28-2001||07:02 PM||||How much power can you get (reliably for the street)?<BR>Who has "proven" performance upgrades? (with contact info)<BR>What all is involved in the swap?<BR>WILL IT BOLT TO THE GETRAG?<BR>Is there a "bolt-on" swap kit for it?<BR>Who has one anywhere near IL?<BR>What are 0-60 and 1/4 mi times?<BR>Anything I forgot?<P>Oh yeah...THANKS!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-28-2001||07:39 PM||||Bob Stieger at Twin Lakes Fiero, Paxton Illinois (see vendor list) just completed a 3800 s/c with the 5 speed last week.  I don't know what that one had for hp rating (220-240 hp from a stock s/c engine), but on the owners initial test drive, they ran into a corn field going a little too fast.  I doubt that you need more performance upgrades.<P>Bob had an automatic one clocked at 153 on the interstate.<P>The swap is easy.  You just need a deep wallet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-28-2001||07:46 PM||||One of the Sessions brothers did a 13.5 a week or so back in his SC3800 -only mod is the smaller pulley from Thresher Racing||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTMike||06-29-2001||04:35 AM||||i also have the same questions.  so anyone that has info would be helping me too.<P>how deep does my wallet need to be.  is it easy to find 3800 s/c engines with low miles on them. how much do they useally go for?<P>any one know what ACE is asking for the complete kit do a self install.    how much would ACE charge. if i found the engine and brough both my car and the engine to them to put it in.   i probably should be emailing ACE about this but i though i would ask here first.  <P>thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||06-29-2001||06:25 AM||||ACE's prices are listed on their web site  <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTMike||06-29-2001||10:50 AM||||thaks for that link   ACE  price listing for the 3800 sc is 2100 bucks for the manual tranny.  they say 4500 for instilations. i'm not sure if that includes the kit to or thats plus the $ 2100 kit.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||06-29-2001||11:41 AM||||Thrashers power tour , Intimidator monte carlo has a very streetable (24mpg) mild cam 370hp 3800SC. The car has the air to liquid intercooler (have to modify a fiero hood) under drive pulley , mild cam , big valve heads , cold air intake , and a few other goodies.<P>I have been thinking the same thing. On the dyno the 3.8SC puts down close to the same #'s as a northstar. Up in here in canada , I can get one with 50,000kms on it for around $2500- $3000. Instead of $5000 for the N*. It all depends on what you want. I don't need it to look that pretty ,I autocross and track the car so this is the main function of an engine conversion for me. I want HP per dollar. (no I don't want a turbo 60 degree motor).<P>The 3.8SC has a good aftermarket behind it, it's one of the best motors in the world according to various publications. <P>Plus blower whine is a nice sound (haha) With the pulley and headers motors are putting down  260+ rear wheel Hp.<P>If anyone has seen the site on the net called Nytemare about a zz4 355hp crate motor in a Fiero , it put down 260 rear wheel Hp (TPI chokes it off) <P>Now anyone have any comments or ideas about ACE's conversion kits?? Phil where are you?? you always tell me to get a 3.8SC. <P>mid 13's and 24mpg+ sounds nice to me. <BR>If you run the #'s , the 3.8SC in a fiero with a getrag puts down 222 rear wheel Hp. Trasher has dyno slips that say there headers add 18 rear wheel hp = 240 rear wheel hp. Multiply that by a 15% driveline loss for power and your in the neighbourhood of 280hp. (other headers may have to be used)<P>I couldn't find any actual #'s for their pulley , but this just goes to show , there is a lot of power hiding in this motor is headers can add 21hp. Slide in a cam and a pulley , I bet your in the neighbourhood of 290 rear wheel hp.<P>remember , each conversion has it's own strong points and it's downfalls. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.thrashercharged.com/Monte_Carlo_htm/monte_carlo.shtm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thrashercharged.com/Monte_Carlo_htm/monte_carlo.shtm</A> <P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">         <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.<P>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 06-29-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRiAD||06-29-2001||02:26 PM||||You guys rock! 5.0 0-60 with just the swaqp and maybe a pulley sounds great, especially knowing all the other mods available! <P>That would put you in Corvette and Carrera territory, blow away all the ricers, and be a great foundation for more!<P>Any other info would also be appreciated!<P>THANKS!||||reg||6
Z||000008||TRiAD||06-29-2001||02:48 PM||||Emailed ACE...here's the reply. <BR>---------------------------<BR>This is on conversion of a 1988 Fiero GT Stick to 3.8 Liter Supercharged 5<BR>spd. Stick. <BR>We will supply conversion parts including:<P>3.8 Liter Supercharged V-6 Engine  (0-15 miles)         $  3,200.00<P>284 Getrag 5 Spd. (Take-outs Unknown Condition)         (Optional)      $ <BR>2,500.00<P>New Shift Cables                                (Optional)      $    <BR>350.00<P>Installation Labor - parts                              $  4,500.00<P>Four Wheel Alignment                            $     100.00<P>A/C Conversion and upgrade to R-134a                    $     525.00<P>Blower Upgrade (Supercharged Only)              (Optional)      $    <BR>250.00<P>Exhaust System Duel - with  Cat. and Muffler Tips               $    <BR>450.00<BR>(There are options available on the exhaust system, please see our web site<BR>for pricing)<P>Stainless Exhaust System Duel -                 (Optional)      $    <BR>800.00<BR>(There are options available on the exhaust system, please see our web site<BR>for pricing).<P>Intercooler Package - Core, manifold, ect.              (Optional)      $ <BR>3,000.00<BR>(This item is Customer installed only, ACE no longer will do in house<BR>installs on the intercooler package).<BR>---------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>---------------------------------------<BR>TOTAL                                           $  8,775.00<BR><B>[$15,675.00 with options]</B><P>Tax rate of 5% will be added to total if dropping your car off and picking<BR>it up at our shop.. Optional equipment not shown in pricing.<P>I hope this answers your questions. If you have any questions, please call.<P>Matt Cutter<BR>-----------------<P><BR>FYI<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||06-29-2001||03:53 PM||||Also, check out West Coast Fiero.  Maybe not for conversion kits, but they can help or do one themselves, and they have headers specially designed for the 3800 in a Fiero.  Nice addition.  <P>Also, Thresher, and RamAir Technologies have performance parts for the 3800SC.  RATech has a 4 door Grand Prix GTP running in the 12s with just bolt ons.  Put that engine in the Fiero and ooooooh baby.  ||||reg||6
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||06-29-2001||03:57 PM||||Yeah , Talk to west coast.<P>A while back I used to talk to a guy who had a black 88GT auto done by West coast. He raved about the quality of the conversion. Unfortunatley the car got smashed beyond repair.<P>I do remember him telling me he beat a 300zx TT quite easily with his conversion and an auto too boot!<P>As for the intercooler , go with thrasher's unit , it's 1/2 the cost @ $1300 , plus you can run a really small blower pulley without fear of detonation on pump gas according to their site.<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||TRiAD||06-29-2001||04:59 PM||||*counting my nickels...*   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||GTMike||06-29-2001||06:23 PM||||i was thinking of finding my own engine. for aound 2000.  <P>then getting ACE kit.  2100 that does include  you sending them your fiero harness and the 3800 harness and they mate the two together and send it back to you.   <P>so you could actually do it your self for around 4100 bucks.   i thihk the bigest place to save money is finding a good deal on an engine.  what cars did the 3800 sc come in?? i'm going to start looking||||reg||1
Z||000013||qwikgta||06-29-2001||07:48 PM||||Make sure to check Ebay, I think there is a 3.8 and a 3.4 on there now.  Also a N* in there too.  Depending on where you live you may find a fourm friend nearby to help the cost of shipping.  they could pick it up for you and then when you get a chance you could make a road trip to pick it up.<P><BR>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||06-29-2001||10:54 PM||||I think if I were to do this, I'd go with ACE's engine, simply because they say they would have 0-13 miles (or something like that) on them. Having a waranted no-mile engine would be worth the trouble for me. <BR>If you do buy a motor from a yard...even a trusted yard, you must always be concerned about condition and longevity. Realistically, it would be best to tear down and rebuild any "used" motor you would buy. <BR>Now...if a friend just wrapped that Bonneville SSEi around a pole, and you could get the 3800SC out of there cheap from him...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||KRMFiero||06-29-2001||11:14 PM||||Well My dad is borrowing his Boss's 1998 Grand prix GTP (with pully) 270 hp right, all factory parts...  this car is you know a nice car but its big - 4 door exc...<P>Well anyways when you turn off TCS and press the porformance shift botton it will lay down 30-40 foot of rubber and hit second gear - its a auto! the car is fast at idle it will cruse at 1k on the highway (foot not even on gas) 3k rpm is 115mph redline is 6k<P>I would love to have this engine in my fiero... thats my next prodject after my Caddy swap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||stimpy||06-30-2001||01:39 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>I think if I were to do this, I'd go with ACE's engine, simply because they say they would have 0-13 miles (or something like that) on them. Having a waranted no-mile engine would be worth the trouble for me. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sure, a zero mile powertrain would be nice. In fact my dad allegedly has one in his 86 GT. However ACE provides ZERO documentation on the engines, and once your car leaves Durango city limits, you are ass-out for any further support.<BR>The "zero-mile, warranteed" powerplant in my dads car required a complete transmission rebuild after about 4k miles. I can tell you the check was not signed by ACE. Also that fancy exhaust system they sell needed to be rewelded due to the lack of any torque strut. (Nevermind the fact it only dumps exhaust out of one side.)<P>Now this was not a budget minded, on the cheap garage job using some ACE parts. This was an in-house conversion and cost was not an object. West Coast Fieros should remember the car, they got to fix a lot of the piss poor engineering of ACE.<P>While I do think that the 3.8 is a kick ass conversion, I wouldn't trust ACE to build a car that I'd need to rely on. My endorsement remains with West Coast Fieros.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||TRiAD||06-30-2001||06:21 AM||||Thanks Stimpy, good to know in advance. <BR>Anyone else have experience with ACE (good or bad)?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000018||GTMike||06-30-2001||06:46 AM||||dose west coast provide a full kit. like ace does.   is wiring up one of these new engines hard to do.  ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Phil||06-30-2001||09:23 AM||||My engine was installed by ACE, however I did add a torque strut(contrary to Rich Cutter I think it is nessessary). 50K miles so far and no problems<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000020||West Coast Fiero||06-30-2001||12:33 PM||||You absolutely have to have a torque strut, or a dog bone as we often refer to it - without it you WILL break mounts.<P> We do not offer a kit per say, however we offer EVERY part to make the swap possible, from mounts, headers, injectors, overdrive pulleys, torque struts... etc. <P> We do wiring as well, however Chris does that in his spare time at home because it is time consuming we do do like to get everything right the first time =-)<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000021||TRiAD||06-30-2001||01:42 PM||||West Coast...I was just getting ready to call you for pricing when I saw your "cinder blocks" post on Archie's thread. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011699.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011699.html</A> <P>I hope you realise there are some people in this world who still appreciate integrity. Go tell your dad you lost a customer over trying to make someone else look bad. <BR>I won't be calling...<p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Slammed Fiero||06-30-2001||04:05 PM||||Sucks to be west coast, I was thinking the same thing. West Coast Does good work from what I hear. Too bad your daddy doesn't regulate your mouth.<BR>the v8 conversion post had nothing to do with you , your just giving your fathers business a bad name<BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000023||gabriel||06-30-2001||04:14 PM||||Hello:<P> &gt;Go tell your dad you lost a customer over trying to make someone else look bad. <P> Hmmm.  My vote for this conversion would still go to West Coast. I like Archie's work, and I definitely respect West Coast's work. <P> As to price on the 3800SC Series II, my cost for the engine from a 97 Olds, complete with wiring harness, PCM, AOD transmission, air handler, canister, and some other stuff was exactly $2,000 delivered.  Runs like H3ll.  I would always rebuild any engine, even if it was just a valve job & hone, just to be sure.  Good luck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||West Coast Fiero||06-30-2001||07:01 PM||||I do appologize for my questions ( not comments ) I had asked Archie, as I see they have evoked the flames of Pennocks. as far as my "daddy" regulating my mouth - I wont even get into that as it is highly probable that that will start another war. I understand that was a comment that was at the top of your head and seemed to work for you, as I most certainly have a "no bullshit tolerance level" - I am down, dirty, and straight to the point - if you havent noticed.<P> We are here to serve the Fiero community and always will be. If you find that my comments and opinions are significantly different from yours let me know - because thats what this forum is all about.<P> I want everyone to know that the comments and opinions expressed and implied from me are those of me, Eric, and no one else here at the shop, unless otherwise stated||||reg||1
Z||000025||TRiAD||06-30-2001||07:29 PM||||<I>"If you find that my comments and opinions are significantly different from yours let me know - because thats what this forum is all about."</I><P>OK, your ignorant (by definition) statement regarding how Archie supports the cars he's working on was WAY out of line. It was a bullsh!t attempt at making someone else who is "dedicated to the Fiero community" look bad. Archie had all the cars there on proper lifts when I visited his shop. <BR>Moral? Don't believe everything you hear...and think before you open your mouth. <BR>Disclaimer or not, you're using the shop name on this forum, so when you talk out your a$$ it makes the shop look bad...real bad. <P>There...now you know. ||||reg||1
