Z||000029||KissMySSFiero||07-01-2001||01:36 AM||||as far as cinder blocks in his video,  i havent seen the video yet.  but tell me this.  how many everyday fiero owners have lifts in their garage?  i dont.  i work on my car at my uncles house.  he has a three car garage with every tool you can imagine.  he has a 55 chevy that runs high 9's in the 1/4 on a 306ci sbc. hes been working on cars for over 35yrs.   id say hes a pretty damn good mechanic.  he doesnt have a lift either. <P>my point is.  archie probably made the video for the regular joe to put a sbc in a fiero.  we dont have lifts at home.  so why would he want to do the swap using a lift.  he probably wanted to do it the way his customers have to do it.  <P><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000030||GTMike||07-01-2001||04:38 AM||||i know i'm new to this board  but  can we stay on topic and have no more posts about cinder blocks.  and more on 3800sc. <P>so eric.  i havn't made up my mind on going with ACE kit.   i actually want to buy the parts that i cant find or make.    you said you sell everything to do the swap.   <BR> <BR>i have done lots of swaps on older carbed cars but none that were efi or used a computer.  i'm deathly afraid of mateing the 2 wireing harnesses my self.  ACE will do it and its included in the cost of the kit. <P>how much would you guys charge to mate the two harnesses together for me and have it all labled to put in.   <P>i can bolt engines to trannies and on to mounts all day long but the electrical i wouldn't know what to do.and would need detailed instructions.  <P>well if you can make out what i was just rambeling about post back with any advice. <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000031||West Coast Fiero||07-01-2001||02:33 PM||||The main reason that we do not offer a kit is that GM changed so many things from flew plates and flywheels, to wiring and basic computer functions from year to year. However we do offer every part needed to install the engine and trans in your car, when it comes down to it, all the conversions are done in house to West Coast Fiero standards as we prefer not to have the customer confused with wiring intigration, smog laws, and computer issues.<P>  I have no problems with ACE, we get to " de-bug" thier installs occasionally, however I had no idea that they dont believe in a torsional strut for the engine, I would look into this to see if it were true or not.<P> And I am shuting my mouth now about Archie - I'll just keep my opinions to myself, as I have many of them.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
